{
  "dom_id": "step-t23017",
  "name": "Estimating Roots",
  "problem": "When we **estimate** a root, we choose one nearby decimal value and check that it is reasonable. Bounds tell us the interval; the estimate tells us which value in that interval is closest.\n\nLet's estimate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/398d865ecee9dba51e8ba4918a187f483b9291ff6ae0d2032be0d95d40190ff7.svg) rounded to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) decimal place. First, we find nearby perfect cubes:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/bca4e36ccfb33070d91ecf1f82eab6ce7d8e06f71d05000633a58ac03ce19107.svg)\nso\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/cdf283b9d6e8644576f4e97abe9203e4115c00fd43314a2323706d1c643e9c0b.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/3636292deb3377b1dfe99da068f300f7dba4ce7fa6acd22164150451dc396ee1.png)\n\nBecause ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/bc98a2fdf686f851fd343e6cca8ebf25186c6d4fe401df573939f8e5e1d5d044.svg) is closer to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/c64ba31f35ed2d1f23f3827854effc6461b82c7cfa7f27694bf545acb565c90a.svg) than to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/f9e10c6abbe30486481349d2f58357e01d37bfd670ed37a29313e8556b57fe2c.svg) we expect ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/398d865ecee9dba51e8ba4918a187f483b9291ff6ae0d2032be0d95d40190ff7.svg) to be closer to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/402ff5d0c0c3aaa47f18c89f6d96c95d47840eac13822d596a51bdb0c5f9a4ab.svg) than to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/9fc073d1e6ebde82eb949a875e40be00b9196e9b14473ee13fa47a26a98d8450.svg) Now, we test nearby tenths:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/4703877c1fc434e00d2fc781d77473c9ce8f775257b953203baa76d914c2458b.svg)\n\nSo, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/5dfbe3c8f263be79d4c240a343aeef3ed741dc5d9a72b0b8c21b38cd9548a66c.svg) To decide which tenth is the better estimate, compare distances from ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/3b3b7808b8023e6edb41eb64eb15e0198ce6843ff72ec8c44e79786e8932dc84.svg)\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/60b754ce1636a8fee75de533c7961f498ac37fd7f6b471971e420985069f3c22.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/bc98a2fdf686f851fd343e6cca8ebf25186c6d4fe401df573939f8e5e1d5d044.svg) is closer to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/9252231dcb743cf6f0c6df56fdcc7e3f30a9c4d371ad30332ac7a5f93b38b3e4.svg) the root is closer to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/106a07431c2edab74f94a851a8f9d6d4c67fb6e29b7c2090e316e5c2032195e3.svg) Therefore,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/5d0fdcc02424b0794c647227784e86791079bbdbc184868c2bbbdec3ddcf86cb.svg)",
